 * a WRITE; everything after the '=' is read. Every other whole-identifier
 * occurrence in a line is a READ -- so "x += 1" and "if (x > 0) {" only read x.
 * An identifier occurrence counts only when the characters around it are not
 * letters, digits, '_' or '$'.
 *
 * parameters(inScope, block) -> the in-scope names that are READ somewhere in the
 *   block, sorted alphabetically (a name only ever written is not a parameter).
 * writes(inScope, block) -> the in-scope names the block writes, in first-write order.
 * returnVariable(inScope, block) -> the single written name, "void" when the block
 *   writes none, and "AMBIGUOUS" when it writes two or more.
